# Production build-time configuration.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* variables into the bundle at `npm run build`, so this
# file has to be present in the checkout the build runs from. The production
# deploy does `git reset --hard origin/main` on the VPS and builds there, so
# committing this file is what makes the value reach the build — a GitHub
# Actions secret would only exist on the runner, which never builds.
#
# This is not a secret. A GA4 measurement ID is served to every visitor inside
# the JS bundle and is readable in any browser's dev tools. It lives here so
# the value is in one place rather than scattered through the source, and so
# development never reports into the production property.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-T8BD5FHMV0
